  "release_date": "2026-07-04T00:00:00Z",
  "updated": "2026-10-28T00:00:00Z",
  "description": "TESSERA v2 is a pixel-wise Sentinel-1/2 foundation model for annual 10m Earth embeddings. A 2B dual-branch Transformer teacher is pretrained with Barlow Twins and mix-up on about 14 billion pixel time series and distilled into four compact students (1-44M parameters) that output 128-d Matryoshka embeddings, whose 16/32/64-d prefixes can be used without retraining. The authors plan to publish precomputed global annual v2 embeddings for 2017-2025, but as of 2026-10-28 they are not yet released: only the model weights are, so users must run a student on their own Sentinel-1/2 time series. In the paper the 44M student beats AlphaEarth, TESSERA v1 and OlmoEarth on a 15-task AlphaEarth suite and a 14-dataset held-out suite.",
  "sci:doi": "10.48550/arXiv.2607.03949",
